quran[20]{c,v,t}:
  50,16,"We indeed created human being, and We know what (doubts) his soul whispers to him. And We are nearer to him than his jugular vein."
  50,17,"When the two receivers (i.e. the two recording angels) record (his deeds), seated on the right side and the left,"
  50,18,"he does not utter a single word, but there is a vigilant observer beside him (to write it down)."
  50,19,"Then, the agony of death comes with the truth. (It is said to him:) ‘This is what you were trying to escape.’"
  50,20,"Then, the Trumpet will be blown: ‘This is the promised Day.’"
  50,21,"Then every soul will come (before Us), accompanied by a driver (pushing it forward) and a witness (to its actions)."
  50,22,"(It will be said to the denier:) ‘Indeed, you were in a state of negligence about this (Day). We have removed your veil (of negligence) from you, and today, your sight is intensely sharp.’"
  50,23,His companion (angel) will say: ‘This is what is ready with me (as a testimony against you).’
  50,24,"(Both angels will be told:) ‘Throw into Hell every stubborn disbeliever,"
  50,25,"(who is) a hinderer of good, a transgressor (and) a doubter,"
  50,26,who has set up another god along with Allah. So the two of you throw him into the severe punishment.’
  50,27,"His companion (Satan) will say: ‘Our Lord! I did not make him rebel. Rather, he was in extreme error (of his own accord).’"
  50,28,"He will say: ‘Do not dispute in My presence, for I had already sent you the warning."
  50,29,"My Word cannot be changed, nor am I unjust to the servants.’"
  50,30,"That Day, We shall say to the Hellfire: ‘Are you full?’ It will say: ‘Are there any more?’"
  50,31,And Paradise will be brought near to the God-conscious; not distant (any longer).
  50,32,"(And they will be told:) ‘This is what you were promised. (It is) for every penitent and dutiful (servant),"
  50,33,who fears the Most-Compassionate (Lord) without seeing (Him) and comes (before His presence) with a penitent heart.
  50,34,Enter it in peace! That is the Day of Eternity.’
  50,35,"There, they will have whatever they wish, and with Us, there is (even) more."
